<title>UK: UK Nationwide raises mortgage rate.</title>
<headline>UK Nationwide raises mortgage rate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Nationwide building society said on Tuesday it had raised its variable mortgage rate to 6.74 percent from 6.49 percent, effective from December 1 1996.  </p>
<p>Other main lenders' variable mortgage rates currently stand at 6.99 percent</p>
<p>The Nationwide added it would increase interest rates on its savings accounts by between 0.1 percent and 0.3 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank of England raised UK base rates by 25 basis points to 6.0 percent on October 30.</p>
</text>
